First for topology I connected PC0, PC1, and PC2 to the wireless's LAN Ethernet ports(1-3) using Copper Straight-Through cables.
The Initial Access was for me enable DHCP on PC0 to find the default geteway (192.168.0.1), then after that I had to log into the router's web GUI using the User name Admin and Password name Admin.
I had to enable the DHCP Setup next. I had to go under basic setup and update the router IP address to 192.168.5.1. I had to update the Start IP address and adjust the max users, and save my settings.
I had to go to the IP configuration and for each computer PC0, PC1, PC2 and renew the DHCP by click on the static first and then back to DHCP. I then had to go to the command line on PC2 and use ipcongfig and ping the gateway 192.168.5.1 and ping the other computers. The pings were successful and all the computers had full connectivity.
Some Challenges I had was that the router's page would timed out at first when right after I saved changes to the new IP. What I did to fix this was I would go into the IP configuration and toggle Static to DHCP to pull the address on the new subnet.
Some things I learned was how to identify and connect the straight-through cable from the PC to the Wireless Lan. I also learned how to use pin and ipconfig to verify network connectivity.
